# Project workflow

The shared project branch is `project-work`. The user explicitly authorized
`phase1-scene-preparation` in an isolated checkout for Phase 1. Continue that
work there; do not create another branch or PR per milestone. Create other
persistent branches only when the user explicitly requests one. Use descriptive
project names without assistant or vendor prefixes.

Before switching, use `git worktree list` to find the intended checkout.
Preserve dirty files, ignored simulation assets and historical experiment data.
Do not reset an existing checkout or move the open paper to a different path.

After a material research decision, append a dated entry to
`docs/RESEARCH_DECISIONS.md`: previous plan, new evidence, choice, implementation
status and next check. Distinguish completed results, interpretations and
proposed experiments. Preserve original model/data/controller provenance;
scientific protocol versions remain distinct even though source shares a branch.

For the Phase 1 walkthrough, present technical choices to the user before
implementing the dependent step. Record approvals and test each approved piece.

Keep `docs/PAPER_PROGRESS.md` and the working manuscript consistent with measured
claims. Compile the existing `.tex` source with the desktop compiler after edits.
